1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 g5 4. h4 g4 5. Ng5 h6 6. Nxf7 Kxf7 7. d4 d5 8. Bxf4
Nf6 9. Nc3 Nc6 {Here Blackburne played 10.e5 in a simul in1894, and Pillsbury
in another simul played 10.Nxd5.} (9... Bb4 10. Be2 Bxc3+ 11. bxc3 Kg6 {
Gunsberg-Marco, Vienna 1903 (0-1)}) 10. exd5 Nxd5 $6 (10... Bd6 $11 {Stockfish
10 (2019)}) 11. Bc4 Be6 $2 12. Nxd5 (12. O-O $18 {Stockfish 10 (2019)}) 12...
Bxd5 13. O-O Bxc4 14. Qxg4 (14. Bxc7+ Bxf1 15. Bxd8 Rxd8 16. Qxf1+ Kg7 17. Qb5
$18 {Stockfish 10 (2019)}) 14... Bxf1 $11 (14... Ke8 $1 $19 {Stockfish 10 
(2019)}) 15. Rxf1 Qxd4+ 16. Be3+ Qf6 17. Qc4+ Kg7 18. Rxf6 Kxf6 19. Qf4+ Ke6
20. Qg4+ Kf6 21. Qf4+ Ke6 {Sources: BCM, October 1953, p266; Illustrated
London News, 6 March 1954 (BH Wood describes it as "the most extraordinary
drawn game of the year")} 1/2-1/2

